From 50c1733e420937b5de067c335860eeb5ac8aba84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SlateX Pipeline <pipeline@slatex.local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:34:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add EXR-derived full-size format; derive plate root from
 shot_plate template

1. Full-size format (project settings): apply_settings() now reads the
   ingested plate's actual EXR dimensions (via a throwaway Read node's
   width()/height(), backed by the file's real displayWindow) and sets
   nuke.root()['format'] to match, registering a new nuke.Format keyed on
   the exact width/height if one doesn't already exist this session. Never
   falls back to a hardcoded resolution (e.g. 1920x1080) - if the plate
   isn't ingested yet or its dimensions can't be read, the script's
   existing format is left untouched and a log line records why. Existing
   FPS/frame-range/color-management behavior is unchanged - the new logic
   is purely additive, gated on the plate already having been resolved for
   the Read-node step.

2. _find_plate_root_dir() no longer hand-joins 'Projects'/'Plates'/
   sequence/shot onto tk.roots['primary'] - that duplicated the
   nfa-shotgun-configuration repo's own shot_plate template logic in a
   second place, and was exactly the kind of drift the folder-structure
   fix in that repo (Artists/Projects becoming their own schema roots,
   {Projectcode} moving to a folder segment) would have silently broken
   here too. Now derives the plate root by resolving the shot_plate
   template itself (context.as_template_fields + apply_fields) and taking
   the parent directory of the resolved file path - so any future
   convention change only needs to happen in templates.yml.

Tests added: tests/test_handler.py, 15 tests using minimal fake nuke/sgtk
modules (no real Nuke/ShotGrid install required) - FPS (SG value, unset,
env-var fallback on SG error), frame range (SG cut fields, unset),
OCIO/color management, format-from-EXR (1080p, 4K, missing file, zero
dimensions, format reuse/no-duplicate, throwaway-node cleanup), and
plate-root-from-template resolution.
